# Line endings. The checks in .pre-commit-config.yaml run on Linux, macOS and
# Windows, and clang-format and shfmt both treat a CRLF file as different from
# its LF twin -- so a Windows checkout that materialized CRLF would fail the same
# hooks that pass everywhere else. Normalizing here is what makes the
# cross-platform promise in doc/coding_standard.md hold.
#
# text=auto leaves git's binary detection alone, so the tracked PNGs and SVGs are
# untouched, and it converts on check-in only -- content already committed with
# CRLF stays as it is. So this renormalizes nothing and dirties no file; it
# governs what enters the repository from here on.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Vendored third-party patch series. Byte-exact by definition: converting an EOL
# inside a patch body changes the hunks and breaks `git apply`. Excluded from the
# linters for the same reason.
patches/** -text
